Third-party components bundled with this application keep their own
original licenses:

- Drum samples: see public/samples/LICENSE.md (mix of CC0 1.0 and
  CC-BY 3.0 — CC-BY attribution requirement documented there and in-app
  under "Datenschutz & Credits").
- Neural Amp Modeler Core (src-tauri/vendor/NeuralAmpModelerCore): MIT
  License, Copyright (c) 2023 Steven Atkinson — see that directory's own
  LICENSE file.
- npm and Cargo dependencies: each under its own published license (see
  package.json / Cargo.toml and each package's own license file).
- LAME MP3 encoder (compiled in via the `mp3lame-encoder`/`mp3lame-sys`
  Cargo crates for native recordings, and via the `@breezystack/lamejs`
  npm package for browser/mobile recordings): LGPL-2.1/LGPL-3.0. Used here
  as a library dependency, not modified or redistributed as its own
  standalone product — the common, low-risk way to use LGPL code. No
  action needed beyond this notice for personal/informal distribution.
- Steinberg ASIO SDK (pulled in transitively via the `asio-sys`/`cpal` Cargo
  dependency, downloaded from steinberg.net at build time — its source is
  not vendored in this repo, only compiled into the final app binary): NOT
  a free-standing open license. As of October 2025 Steinberg dual-licenses
  it as GPLv3 (requires this whole app to also be GPLv3/source-available)
  or a proprietary license that is free of charge but requires signing
  Steinberg's own "Proprietary ASIO SDK License Agreement" before
  distributing any product built against the SDK. This has NOT been done
  for Pocket Studio yet — unresolved, needs the app's owner to review
  https://www.steinberg.net/developers/ and either sign that agreement or
  choose the GPLv3 path before handing the Windows build to anyone beyond
  personal use.

This is a placeholder license reflecting the project's current status as
a personal project shared informally with a small number of people. It is
not a substitute for legal advice — if this project ever moves toward
